  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG2_U06_L06_Q01</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> ALG2_U06_L06_Q01</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.A2.FM.1; MLA.A2.EX.4; MLA.A2.FN.2 (modeling synthesis)</p><p>A fundraiser has $200 and earns $15 per item. Which expression models total money after x items?</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[200+15x]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Correct. Add starting money and earnings per item.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[200x+15]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This treats the starting money as the per-item rate.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[15x-200]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This subtracts the starting amount incorrectly.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[200/15x]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This does not represent repeated item earnings.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG2_U06_L06_Q02</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> ALG2_U06_L06_Q02</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.A2.FM.1; MLA.A2.EX.4; MLA.A2.FN.2 (modeling synthesis)</p><p>Which inequality represents needing at least 1000 dollars?</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[M &lt; 1000]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This means less than 1000, not at least.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[M &gt;= 1000]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Correct. At least means greater than or equal to.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[M = 1000 only]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[At least includes 1000 and values greater than 1000.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[M &lt;= 1000]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This means no more than 1000.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG2_U06_L06_Q03</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> ALG2_U06_L06_Q03</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.A2.FM.1; MLA.A2.EX.4; MLA.A2.FN.2 (modeling synthesis)</p><p>Solve 250+20x &gt;= 850.</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[x &gt;= 20]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This subtracts incorrectly or divides before isolating.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[x &gt;= 25]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This does not account for the full difference from 250 to 850.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[x &gt;= 30]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Correct. 20x &gt;= 600, so x &gt;= 30.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[x &gt;= 55]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This adds 250 and 850 before dividing.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG2_U06_L06_Q04</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> ALG2_U06_L06_Q04</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.A2.FM.1; MLA.A2.EX.4; MLA.A2.FN.2 (modeling synthesis)</p><p>A calculation gives 12.4 buses needed. How many buses are needed?</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[12]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Rounding down leaves some people without a bus.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[12.4]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[A fractional bus is not realistic.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[13.4]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[The count should be a whole number.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[13]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Correct. Bus counts must be whole numbers, and the constraint requires rounding up.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG2_U06_L06_Q05</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> ALG2_U06_L06_Q05</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.A2.FM.1; MLA.A2.EX.4; MLA.A2.FN.2 (modeling synthesis)</p><p>Which is an assumption in a simple savings model?</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[The rate stays the same over the time period.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Correct. Many simple models assume a constant rate.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[The answer has no units.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Units are not an assumption; they are required for interpretation.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[The model cannot be checked.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Models should be checked against context.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[The variables are meaningless.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Variables should have clear meanings.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG2_U06_L06_Q06</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> ALG2_U06_L06_Q06</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.A2.FM.1; MLA.A2.EX.4; MLA.A2.FN.2 (modeling synthesis)</p><p>What is a constraint?</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[A random guess]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[A constraint is based on context, not guessing.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[A limit or requirement from the context]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Correct. Constraints restrict possible solutions.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[The color of the graph]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Graph color is not a mathematical constraint.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[A deleted variable]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Variables are defined and used, not deleted.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG2_U06_L06_Q07</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> ALG2_U06_L06_Q07</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.A2.FM.1; MLA.A2.EX.4; MLA.A2.FN.2 (modeling synthesis)</p><p>Why should units be included in a final answer?</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Units make every answer larger.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Units do not change numerical size.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Units replace calculations.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Calculations are still needed.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Units explain what the number represents.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Correct. Units connect the result to the context.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Units are optional in modeling.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Units are essential for interpretation.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG2_U06_L06_Q08</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> ALG2_U06_L06_Q08</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.A2.FM.1; MLA.A2.EX.4; MLA.A2.FN.2 (modeling synthesis)</p><p>A model predicts negative time. What should you do?</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Accept it because equations are always right.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[A mathematical answer must still make sense in context.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Change time to money.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Changing units does not fix the invalid result.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Ignore the negative sign.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[The sign is part of the solution and must be interpreted.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Reject or revise it because time cannot be negative in the context.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Correct. Context makes negative time invalid.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG2_U06_L06_Q09</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> ALG2_U06_L06_Q09</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.A2.FM.1; MLA.A2.EX.4; MLA.A2.FN.2 (modeling synthesis)</p><p>Which is the best first step in modeling?</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Understand the context and define variables.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Correct. Variables and context guide the model.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Solve before reading the question.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Solving requires a model and defined variables.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Round all numbers immediately.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Rounding too early can distort the model.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Ignore constraints until after submission.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Constraints must be considered before finalizing.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG2_U06_L06_Q10</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> ALG2_U06_L06_Q10</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.A2.FM.1; MLA.A2.EX.4; MLA.A2.FN.2 (modeling synthesis)</p><p>A model P=500(1.08)ᵗ predicts population. What does 1.08 mean?</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[108 people are added each year.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[The factor represents percent growth, not a fixed count.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[The population grows by 8% each time period.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Correct. A factor of 1.08 means 8% growth.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[The initial population is 1.08.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[The initial population is 500.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[The time period is 1.08 years.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[The exponent t represents time periods.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG2_U06_L06_Q11</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> ALG2_U06_L06_Q11</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.A2.FM.1; MLA.A2.EX.4; MLA.A2.FN.2 (modeling synthesis)</p><p>A habitat can support at most 1,000 animals. A model predicts 1,150. What is the issue?</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[The model has no output.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[The model does have an output.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[The prediction is below capacity.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[1150 is above 1000, so the prediction is not below the habitat capacity.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[The prediction violates the maximum constraint.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Correct. The model output is greater than the habitat limit.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[The input must be negative.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[The issue is the output constraint, not input sign.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG2_U06_L06_Q12</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> ALG2_U06_L06_Q12</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.A2.FM.1; MLA.A2.EX.4; MLA.A2.FN.2 (modeling synthesis)</p><p>What is model validation?</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Making the answer longer]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Length does not validate a model.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Removing all assumptions]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Assumptions should be checked, not simply removed.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Choosing the first equation available]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Validation requires evidence.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Checking whether the model works for the context and data]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Correct. Validation tests reasonableness and fit.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG2_U06_L06_Q13</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> ALG2_U06_L06_Q13</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.A2.FM.1; MLA.A2.EX.4; MLA.A2.FN.2 (modeling synthesis)</p><p>A taxi charges $4 plus $2.50 per mile. Which model gives cost C for m miles?</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[C=4+2.50m]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Correct. The fixed fee is added to the per-mile charge.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[C=4m+2.50]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This swaps the fixed fee and per-mile rate.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[C=2.50/m+4]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This rational expression does not model repeated miles.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[C=4(2.50)ᵐ]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This is exponential and does not match a per-mile fee.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG2_U06_L06_Q14</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> ALG2_U06_L06_Q14</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.A2.FM.1; MLA.A2.EX.4; MLA.A2.FN.2 (modeling synthesis)</p><p>Using C=4+2.50m, what is the cost for 8 miles?</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[$20]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This uses only the per-mile charge.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[$24]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Correct. C=4+2.50(8)=24.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[$32]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This multiplies the fixed fee by miles.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[$10.50]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This adds 4, 2.50, and 8 without applying the model.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG2_U06_L06_Q15</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> ALG2_U06_L06_Q15</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.A2.FM.1; MLA.A2.EX.4; MLA.A2.FN.2 (modeling synthesis)</p><p>Which answer best interprets x &gt;= 30 in a ticket-selling model?</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Sell exactly 30 tickets only.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Greater values also satisfy the inequality.]]></text>
